\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Canary sensor validation on Llama-3.1-8B (TP=$2$). (a)\nobreakspace  {}Signal magnitude (log scale): max $\hat  {\delta }_4$ vs the cache-relative canary's warmup reading, $\sim 550\times $ larger. (b)\nobreakspace  {}Batch-size invariance: mns=$1$ vs mns=$8$ max ratio is $1.21\times $. (c)\nobreakspace  {}Cross-tier monotonicity: $\hat  {\delta }_2 \geq \hat  {\delta }_4$ holds for every layer (no points below the dashed identity line). (d)\nobreakspace  {}Cross-seed stability: $\rho {=}0.876$ between per-layer rankings at seeds $0$ and $7$.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sensor}{{2}{5}{Canary sensor validation on Llama-3.1-8B (TP=$2$). (a)~Signal magnitude (log scale): max $\hat {\delta }_4$ vs the cache-relative canary's warmup reading, $\sim 550\times $ larger. (b)~Batch-size invariance: mns=$1$ vs mns=$8$ max ratio is $1.21\times $. (c)~Cross-tier monotonicity: $\hat {\delta }_2 \geq \hat {\delta }_4$ holds for every layer (no points below the dashed identity line). (d)~Cross-seed stability: $\rho {=}0.876$ between per-layer rankings at seeds $0$ and $7$}{figure.2}{}}
