\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Cross-workload comparison on Llama-3.1-70B with the controller live throughout serving. (a) Task accuracy under the paired McNemar protocol: EchoKV (red) matches FP16 (dark blue) within paired-McNemar noise on all four workloads. KIVI-INT4 shows a measurable $4$-bit deficit on GSM8K-Hard ($p{=}0.052$) and on $\tau $-Bench ($\Delta {=}{-}0.040$). (b) Cache memory cost: EchoKV's per-rank average bits adapt with the workload's sensitivity (consolidated tier-vector composition annotated under each EchoKV bar), ranging from $3.97$ on RULER@128K to $6.54$ on $\tau $-Bench (airline + retail).}}{7}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cross_workload}{{3}{7}{Cross-workload comparison on Llama-3.1-70B with the controller live throughout serving. (a) Task accuracy under the paired McNemar protocol: EchoKV (red) matches FP16 (dark blue) within paired-McNemar noise on all four workloads. KIVI-INT4 shows a measurable $4$-bit deficit on GSM8K-Hard ($p{=}0.052$) and on $\tau $-Bench ($\Delta {=}{-}0.040$). (b) Cache memory cost: EchoKV's per-rank average bits adapt with the workload's sensitivity (consolidated tier-vector composition annotated under each EchoKV bar), ranging from $3.97$ on RULER@128K to $6.54$ on $\tau $-Bench (airline + retail)}{figure.3}{}}
